diff --git a/volume-cartographer/utils/VERIFIED_CT_READS.md b/volume-cartographer/utils/VERIFIED_CT_READS.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..1493110
--- /dev/null
+++ b/volume-cartographer/utils/VERIFIED_CT_READS.md
@@ -0,0 +1,17 @@
+# Draft opt-in verification of CT reads
+
+This CPU-only opt-in draft targets Villa base `417e17689029434fa1572efe20a3e7a9bfc79be4`. It leaves the default read path unchanged. Production activation requires a caller-side ledger acceptance gate and review of the exact application integration.
+
+Repeated whole-volume verification of a restored CT dataset dominated preparation of small real scroll crops. The optional reader verifies the same owned compressed bytes returned to the decoder, using a complete immutable manifest. With no opt-in environment the existing read path remains unchanged. OpenSSL Crypto supplies SHA256; no custom digest implementation is introduced.
+
+Set all three environment variables together: `VC_VERIFIED_CT_MANIFEST`, `VC_VERIFIED_CT_MANIFEST_SHA256`, and a fresh owned `VC_VERIFIED_CT_LEDGER`. The manifest schema is `verified-ct-read-manifest-v1`, with canonical `volume_root`, complete `objects` records containing `key`, `absent`, `bytes`, and `sha256`, and `max_chunk_bytes` in the range 1 byte through 32 MiB. The retained CT manifest declares a 2 MiB limit and its largest present chunk is 2 MiB; the compiled 32 MiB ceiling gives 16x headroom while bounding the per-read buffer allocation. This is a CT-specific bound, not a promise to accept arbitrarily large Zarr chunks. Explicit absence is separate from a missing/unlisted object. Protected shard and mmap entry points reject rather than bypass verification. The caller must keep the volume tree immutable throughout guarded reads: the guard rejects symlinks it observes and verifies the digest of the exact owned bytes it returns, but does not claim race-free filesystem confinement against concurrent path replacement. With `VC_VERIFIED_CT_MANIFEST` enabled, Store-backed Zarr access is rejected process-wide: Store open overloads do not yet have a canonical array root to check, so the restriction also applies to unrelated Store roots. This opt-in supports the guarded filesystem Zarr2 G0 path; remove all three opt-in variables to use stock Store access. This is not universal I/O interception.
+
+A renderer may catch decoding exceptions and zero-fill. Therefore a production caller MUST audit the ledger before accepting science: exact INITIALIZED manifest binding, nonzero VERIFIED read coverage, no REJECTED event, and bounded complete evidence. Mandatory evidence infrastructure failures terminate with code86 without a core dump. The standalone library cannot make an application-level acceptance decision on a swallowed read failure.
+
+## Tests and real-data evidence
+
+Enable the existing CMake `VC_TESTING` option and run `ctest -R verified_ct_read --output-on-failure` after building `test_verified_ct_read`. Tests exercise actual public Zarr API calls, exact bytes, mutation/size/absence, forbidden bypasses, mandatory evidence failures, both Store-open overloads with a real unrelated `FileSystemStore`, and stock Store reads in children with all opt-in variables removed. The earlier focused central CMake/CTest run passed the original fixture (1/1 CTest, 18 public-API cases) against the separately qualified imported library; it did not run this revised fixture or configure the full repository. Re-run the revised CPU-only fixture in the PR build environment. macOS/arm64 are not qualified.
+
+Earlier real-data qualification and nine-pair results belong to older source revisions and are not evidence for this final combined patch. The final-source CPU-only comparison used three AB/BA/AB pairs on two fixed crops; all six arms passed exact complete-tree comparison. Median stock/candidate times were 52.690/5.052 seconds (27×180×1060; 10.43×) and 54.203/5.558 seconds (27×180×4640; 9.75×); summed two-crop pair ratios were 9.64×, 9.71×, and 10.08×. These are fixed-workload CPU preparation observations, not GPU, full-pipeline, or universal speedups. PawPad services and a production controller/validator were active during measurement, limiting timing precision. The final-source-v2 summary, receipt, and linker proof are retained separately in the takeover evidence workspace.
+
+The two-crop CPU process sum was about59Ã¢â‚¬â€œ64 seconds stock and10.6Ã¢â‚¬â€œ11.1 seconds candidate in a warm-cache test. These are CPU component observations, not GPU/full-pipeline speedups. One RTX-labelled CPU repetition overlapped cross-host archive reads. Native correctness runs were nonisolated, and strict RTX performance ownership remains unresolved. Transfer, queue wait and unavailable source-pin preflight clocks are not silently summed into an invented end-to-end benchmark. No production verification was removed by this draft.
diff --git a/volume-cartographer/utils/src/verified_chunk_read.hpp b/volume-cartographer/utils/src/verified_chunk_read.hpp
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..507e712
--- /dev/null
+++ b/volume-cartographer/utils/src/verified_chunk_read.hpp
@@ -0,0 +1,86 @@
+#pragma once
+// Prospective guard for utils::ZarrArray::read_raw, NOT a universal I/O hook.
+#include <cstddef>
+#include <filesystem>
+#include <fstream>
+#include <functional>
+#include <map>
+#include <optional>
+#include <stdexcept>
+#include <string>
+#include <vector>
+
+namespace selected_read {
+using Bytes = std::vector<std::byte>;
+struct Expected { bool absent; std::size_t size; std::string sha256; };
+class Guard {
+ static constexpr std::size_t kMaxVerifiedChunkBytes = 32u * 1024u * 1024u;
+ std::filesystem::path volume_, group_;
+ std::map<std::string, Expected> manifest_;
+ std::function<std::string(const Bytes&)> digest_;
+ std::size_t max_bytes_;
+ [[noreturn]] static void fail(const char* why) { throw std::runtime_error(why); }
+public:
+ Guard(std::filesystem::path volume, std::map<std::string, Expected> manifest,
+       std::function<std::string(const Bytes&)> digest, std::size_t max_bytes)
+ : volume_(std::filesystem::canonical(volume)), group_(volume_/"0"),
+   manifest_(std::move(manifest)), digest_(std::move(digest)), max_bytes_(max_bytes) {
+  // The retained CT manifest uses 2 MiB chunks. A 32 MiB hard ceiling leaves
+  // 16x headroom while keeping malformed manifests from requesting unbounded
+  // per-read allocations. The schema is for this guarded CT path, not arbitrary
+  // user-selected Zarr chunk sizes.
+  if (!max_bytes_ || max_bytes_ > kMaxVerifiedChunkBytes || !digest_) fail("guard configuration");
+  for (const auto& [k,v]:manifest_) {
+   std::filesystem::path p(k);
+   if (k.empty() || p.is_absolute() || p.lexically_normal()!=p) fail("manifest key");
+   for (auto& part:p) if (part==".." || part==".") fail("manifest escape");
+   if (v.absent ? (v.size!=0 || !v.sha256.empty()) :
+       (v.size>max_bytes_ || v.sha256.size()!=64 ||
+        v.sha256.find_first_not_of("0123456789abcdef")!=std::string::npos)) fail("manifest value");
+  }
+ }
+ bool protects(const std::filesystem::path& root) const {
+  auto r=std::filesystem::weakly_canonical(root);
+  auto rel=r.lexically_relative(volume_);
+  return r==volume_ || (!rel.empty() && *rel.begin()!="..");
+ }
+ // Call this on EVERY read_raw before choosing store_/filesystem branches.
+ // Returns the exact compressed byte vector subsequently given to the decoder.
+ std::optional<Bytes> read(const std::filesystem::path& root, const std::string& key,
+                           bool sharded=false, bool alternate_store=false) const {
+  if (!protects(root)) fail("guard called outside protected volume");
+  if (sharded || alternate_store) fail("unsupported protected storage bypass");
+  if (std::filesystem::weakly_canonical(root)!=group_) fail("unapproved CT level");
+  std::filesystem::path relative(key);
+  if (key.empty() || relative.is_absolute() || relative.lexically_normal()!=relative) fail("read key");
+  for (auto& part:relative) if (part==".." || part==".") fail("read escape");
+  auto row=manifest_.find(key);
+  if (row==manifest_.end()) fail("unlisted CT read");
+  auto file=group_/relative;
+  // Reject symlink components observed before open. The caller must keep the
+  // input tree immutable for the guarded operation; the digest authenticates
+  // the exact owned bytes returned even if the filesystem path is later changed.
+  auto cursor=group_;
+  for (auto& part:relative) { cursor/=part; if (std::filesystem::is_symlink(std::filesystem::symlink_status(cursor))) fail("chunk symlink"); }
+  const auto& expected=row->second;
+  if (expected.absent) {
+   if (std::filesystem::exists(file)) fail("source-absent chunk appeared");
+   return std::nullopt;
+  }
+  if (!std::filesystem::is_regular_file(file)) fail("present chunk missing/nonregular");
+  if (std::filesystem::file_size(file)!=expected.size) fail("chunk size mismatch");
+  std::ifstream stream(file,std::ios::binary);
+  if (!stream) fail("chunk open");
+  Bytes bytes(expected.size);
+  if (expected.size && !stream.read(reinterpret_cast<char*>(bytes.data()),bytes.size())) fail("chunk short read");
+  char extra;
+  if (stream.get(extra) || !stream.eof()) fail("chunk changed/error during read");
+  if (digest_(bytes)!=expected.sha256) fail("chunk SHA256 mismatch");
+  return bytes; // immutable owned snapshot; no hash-then-reopen window.
+ }
+ // Must be called at entry of mmap/shard/alternate-store APIs, before any I/O.
+ void reject_bypass(const std::filesystem::path& root) const {
+  if (protects(root)) fail("protected bypass API forbidden");
+ }
+};
+}
diff --git a/volume-cartographer/utils/src/verified_chunk_runtime.hpp b/volume-cartographer/utils/src/verified_chunk_runtime.hpp
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..0521be6
--- /dev/null
+++ b/volume-cartographer/utils/src/verified_chunk_runtime.hpp
@@ -0,0 +1,86 @@
+#pragma once
+#include "verified_chunk_read.hpp"
+#include <cstdlib>
+#include <mutex>
+#include <memory>
+#include <cstdio>
+extern "C" unsigned char* SHA256(const unsigned char*,std::size_t,unsigned char*);
+namespace selected_read {
+// Opt-in integrity evidence is mandatory. A decoder may catch C++ exceptions
+// and substitute zeroes, so evidence infrastructure failures must not unwind.
+[[noreturn]] inline void evidence_fatal() noexcept {
+ std::fputs("selected-read mandatory evidence failure\n",stderr);
+ std::fflush(stderr);std::_Exit(86);
+}
+inline std::string sha256(const Bytes& b) {
+ unsigned char digest[32];SHA256(reinterpret_cast<const unsigned char*>(b.data()),b.size(),digest);
+ const char* hex="0123456789abcdef";std::string out;
+ for(auto x:digest){out+=hex[x>>4];out+=hex[x&15];}return out;
+}
+class Runtime {
+ std::unique_ptr<Guard> guard_;
+ std::filesystem::path ledger_;
+ std::mutex ledger_mutex_;
+ std::size_t events_=0;
+ void event(const std::string& status,const std::string& key,std::size_t size) {
+  try {
+  std::lock_guard<std::mutex> lock(ledger_mutex_);
+  if(++events_>65536)throw std::runtime_error("bounded verification ledger exceeded");
+  utils::Json e=utils::Json::object();e["status"]=status;e["key"]=key;e["bytes"]=uint64_t(size);
+  std::ofstream f(ledger_,std::ios::app);f<<e.dump()<<'\n';f.flush();
+  if(!f)throw std::runtime_error("verification ledger write");
+  } catch(...) { evidence_fatal(); }
+ }
+public:
+ Runtime() {
+  const char* manifest=std::getenv("VC_VERIFIED_CT_MANIFEST");
+  const char* expected=std::getenv("VC_VERIFIED_CT_MANIFEST_SHA256");
+  const char* ledger=std::getenv("VC_VERIFIED_CT_LEDGER");
+  if(!manifest && !expected && !ledger) return; // Stock mode only when every opt-in variable is absent.
+  if(!manifest || !expected || !ledger) evidence_fatal();
+  std::ifstream f(manifest,std::ios::binary|std::ios::ate);
+  auto size=f.tellg();if(!f || size<0 || size>32*1024*1024)throw std::runtime_error("bounded manifest");
+  Bytes bytes(static_cast<std::size_t>(size));f.seekg(0);
+  if(size && !f.read(reinterpret_cast<char*>(bytes.data()),size))throw std::runtime_error("manifest read");
+  if(sha256(bytes)!=expected)throw std::runtime_error("manifest SHA256");
+  auto j=utils::Json::parse(std::string(reinterpret_cast<char*>(bytes.data()),bytes.size()));
+  if(j.at("schema").get_string()!="verified-ct-read-manifest-v1")throw std::runtime_error("manifest schema");
+  std::map<std::string,Expected> records;
+  for(const auto& r:j.at("objects")) {
+   auto key=r.at("key").get_string();
+   if(!records.emplace(key,Expected{r.at("absent").get_bool(),r.at("bytes").get_size_t(),r.at("sha256").get_string()}).second)
+    throw std::runtime_error("duplicate CT manifest key");
+  }
+  if(records.empty())throw std::runtime_error("empty CT manifest");
+  ledger_=ledger;
+  guard_=std::make_unique<Guard>(j.at("volume_root").get_string(),std::move(records),sha256,j.at("max_chunk_bytes").get_size_t());
+  event("INITIALIZED",expected,0);
+ }
+ bool protects(const std::filesystem::path& root)const{return guard_ && guard_->protects(root);}
+ void reject_store() {
+  if(guard_){try{event("REJECTED_STORE","alternate-store",0);}catch(...){};throw std::runtime_error("alternate store forbidden in guarded qualification");}
+ }
+ std::optional<Bytes> read(const std::filesystem::path& root,const std::string& key,bool shard,bool store) {
+  try {
+   auto bytes=guard_->read(root,key,shard,store);
+   event(bytes?"VERIFIED_PRESENT":"EXPLICIT_ABSENT",key,bytes?bytes->size():0);
+   return bytes;
+  } catch(...) {
+   // Preserve the primary verification failure if evidence storage also fails.
+   try{event("REJECTED",key,0);}catch(...){}
+   throw;
+  }
+ }
+ void reject(const std::filesystem::path& root) {
+  if(protects(root)){try{event("REJECTED_BYPASS",root.string(),0);}catch(...){};guard_->reject_bypass(root);}
+ }
+};
+inline Runtime& runtime(){
+ static Runtime value=[]() -> Runtime {
+  // A missing env retains stock behavior; an applied but invalid opt-in cannot
+  // silently fall back after a renderer catches initialization exceptions.
+  try {return Runtime();} catch(...) {evidence_fatal();}
+ }();
+ return value;
+}
+}
